      <abstract>
        <para>
          &rear; (&rear.long;) is a disaster recovery framework that helps system administrators
          re-create Linux infrastructure after a system failure. Using &rear;, you can create a
          bootable recovery system that re-creates the failed system's storage layout, restores
          files from a backup, and reinstalls the boot loader. To recover from a disaster as
          quickly as possible, prepare a disaster recovery system <emphasis>before</emphasis> the
          disaster happens and test it regularly on identical test hardware.
        </para>
        <para><emphasis role="bold">Prerequisites</emphasis></para>
        <itemizedlist>
          <listitem><para>Two systems: the machine to back up and an identical test machine.
          <quote>Identical</quote> in this context means that you can, for example, replace a
          network card with another one using the same kernel driver.</para></listitem>
          <listitem><para>An internal backup tool, such as <command>tar</command>, or a supported
          third-party backup tool.</para></listitem>
        </itemizedlist>
      </abstract>
